##
## This project's own validation messages, below.
##
## They are hand-maintained rather than extracted. `mix gettext.extract` reads
## literal `dgettext/3` calls, and the only call for this domain is in
## `HospitalityComsWeb.ErrorEnvelope`, where the msgid is a runtime value — the
## message a changeset carries. So extraction cannot see these, and it does not
## remove them either: it writes a `.pot` only for a domain it found messages
## in, and it finds none here. Adding a validation message means adding a line
## here and running `mix gettext.merge priv/gettext`.
##
## Messages that bake a bound into the string are deliberately absent. A
## `check_constraint/3` error carries no `count` binding — Ecto's API has
## nowhere to put one — so its msgid would have to vary with the constant and
## could never be translated. Those are the database's backstop for writes that
## never meet a changeset, unreachable from the API because the changeset
## refuses first, and they stay in English.
